<title>USA: P&amp;G grants ulcer drug license to Glaxo.</title>
<headline>P&amp;G grants ulcer drug license to Glaxo.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Procter &amp; Gamble Co said on Monday it has granted a worldwide license to Glaxo Wellcome Plc, involving four patents for P&amp;G's ulcer eradication drug technology.</p>
<p>This license allows Glaxo Wellcome to sell certain ulcer drug therapies and, in return, Glaxo will make payments to P&amp;G based on sales of Glaxo Wellcome's H. pylori treatment products in countries where P&amp;G has valid patents.  </p>
<p>Glaxo Wellcome markets ranitidine bismuth citrate, sold under the brand names Tritec and Pylorid, along with anti-infectives for the treatment of duodenal ulcer disease caused by H. pylori, the company said.</p>
</text>
